BT
/F1 22 Tf 50 790 Td (MummyAI Project Proposal) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 760 Td (Maternal, Child Health & Development Companion) Tj
/F2 10 Tf 50 738 Td (Project status: Early-stage prototype for education and organization; not a medical device.) Tj
/F1 16 Tf 50 710 Td (Executive Summary) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 690 Td (MummyAI is a privacy-first digital companion for maternal and child health. It supports) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 675 Td (families with pregnancy planning, appointment tracking, developmental observations, and) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 660 Td (simple health education without replacing clinical judgment.) Tj
/F1 16 Tf 50 628 Td (Problem and Opportunity) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 608 Td (? Families manage information across paper notes, mobile apps, and clinic communication.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 593 Td (? Pregnancy and childhood care require coordinated appointments, growth tracking, and) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 578 Td (  immunization records.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 563 Td (? Language and literacy barriers make reliable health information harder to access.) Tj
/F1 16 Tf 50 531 Td (Target Users) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 511 Td (? Pregnant mothers and caregivers) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 496 Td (? Parents tracking growth, immunization, and developmental milestones) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 481 Td (? Midwives, clinicians, and specialists using consent-based summaries) Tj
/F1 16 Tf 50 449 Td (Product Vision) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 429 Td (The long-term vision is a single family-centered platform spanning pregnancy, birth, and) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 414 Td (childhood. It combines structured records, multilingual access, safe AI assistance, and) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 399 Td (approved educational content while preserving professional oversight.) Tj
/F1 16 Tf 50 367 Td (Core Features) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 347 Td (? Maternal health records, antenatal tracking, and follow-up planning) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 332 Td (? Birth and newborn records, feeding support, and discharge information) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 317 Td (? Child growth, immunization, appointments, and developmental notes) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 302 Td (? Restricted AI assistant for education, clinic-question preparation, and synthetic records) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 16 Tf 50 790 Td (System Architecture) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 770 Td (Frontend: React + Vite client for families and future professional workflows.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 755 Td (Backend: Express API with validation, security headers, and rate limits.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 740 Td (AI Layer: Local Ollama tool-calling orchestration with a narrow allowlist of approved tools.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 725 Td (Data: Optional MongoDB Atlas for synthetic-only demo records with strict read-only filtering.) Tj
/F1 16 Tf 50 693 Td (Safety and Governance) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 673 Td (? The system is not a substitute for professional clinical care.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 658 Td (? AI must not diagnose, prescribe, or make treatment decisions autonomously.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 643 Td (? Real patient data is not used in the prototype; all data handling is synthetic by default.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 628 Td (? Authentication, caregiver authorization, and audit logging are required before real-world use.) Tj
/F1 16 Tf 50 596 Td (Roadmap) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 576 Td (Phase 0: Starter frontend, backend, README, and safety notes complete.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 561 Td (Phase 1: Profile forms, authentication, privacy controls, and record access design.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 546 Td (Phase 2: Trusted AI, schema validation, synthetic record tools, and approved knowledge retrieval.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 531 Td (Phase 3: Growth monitoring, reminders, immunization support, and professional review workflows.) Tj
/F1 16 Tf 50 499 Td (Next Steps) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 479 Td (1. Finalize UX flows for family and clinician use.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 464 Td (2. Implement secure authentication and caregiver authorization boundaries.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 449 Td (3. Add measurement validation and consent-controlled record access.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 434 Td (4. Establish approved knowledge sources and run safety/privacy reviews before pilot.) Tj
/F2 10 Tf 50 70 Td (Prepared for the MummyAI project using project documentation and architecture notes.) Tj
